WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.182 --> 00:00:02.060
(audience applauds)
- Welcome back to Drew's News.

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:03.020
Rossy, what's next?

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.490
- Well, we got another dream job listing.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:06.323
Listen to this.

00:00:06.323 --> 00:00:08.620
Mental Floss reports a
company called Petable

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:13.000
will pay you $1000 to watch
a bunch of dog movies.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.450
Uh, anyone in? Hello?

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:15.859
- [Drew] Sign me up!
(audience applauds)

00:00:15.859 --> 00:00:17.310
Yeah, exactly.
- Right?

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.700
- And here's how it breaks down.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.760
You get $100 an hour to watch six movies.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.390
And they are "Marley and Me."

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.223
- [Audience] Aww.

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:25.056
- Aww, I know!

00:00:25.056 --> 00:00:26.800
"A Dog's Journey."

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.633
Uh-huh.

00:00:27.633 --> 00:00:29.487
"Because of Winn-Dixie," "Eight Below,"

00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:33.080
"Lady and the Tramp" and
"The Call of the Wild."

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.820
And they'll cover all the rental costs.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.913
But you're responsible
for your own tissues.

00:00:36.913 --> 00:00:37.746
(audience laughs)

00:00:37.746 --> 00:00:40.341
Because some of those
movies are rrrr-ough!

00:00:40.341 --> 00:00:41.880
(audience laughs)

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:42.713
Stupid.

00:00:42.713 --> 00:00:44.190
But I will say they missed...

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.710
Can I just throw out
"Beverly Hills Chihuahua?"

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:47.543
Please!
(audience applauds)

00:00:47.543 --> 00:00:49.030
I love that movie so much.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.470
And I know, I know...

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:51.940
- I'm so steaming mad!

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.300
They didn't call me for the sequel.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.617
I tried, I worked really hard on Chloe!

00:00:57.617 --> 00:01:00.179
- "Beverly Hills Chihuahua,"
talk about an Oscar movie.

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:01.998
I'm voting for that.
(audience applauds)

00:01:01.998 --> 00:01:03.190
I loved it.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:05.960
And in all the things
you've done in your career,

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.480
being a voice in "Beverly Hills Chihuahua"

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:10.500
is one of my, I'm most
jealous of that, I think.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.960
- Well, 'cause you have
chihuahuas, that's why.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.500
- Yes, and I have studied them, Drew.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:15.980
I know how to be a chihuahua.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.120
- Well, then, you know what?

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.075
- [Ross] What?

00:01:18.075 --> 00:01:18.908
- Rex Reed!

00:01:18.908 --> 00:01:21.730
I'd love to know how you
thought I did actually.

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:23.370
In all earnestness.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:25.590
Maybe there's a reason
I didn't get called back

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.100
for the second movie.
(audience laughs)

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.250
- Listen, I thought you were great,

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.640
and I'm not just throwing you a bone.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.128
(audience laughs)

00:01:32.128 --> 00:01:34.010
- What would your favorite
dog movie be, Rossy?

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.474
- Of all time?

00:01:35.474 --> 00:01:37.010
Besides that?

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:38.100
Probably "Lady and the Tramp,"

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.970
I think that's why I
love spaghetti so much,

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:41.450
is because of that movie, yeah.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.242
- You and Welly nose to
nose on the pasta strand.

00:01:44.242 --> 00:01:45.140
- Awww, man.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.600
Except ours would be
like, a zucchini noodle,

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.100
'cause I'm trying to keep
it together for the wedding.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.070
- It would totally be a zoodle, Ross!

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.410
- A total zoodle.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.270
- I would have to pick "Marley and Me."

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:54.493
That movie is one of my
favorite movies ever made.

00:01:54.493 --> 00:01:58.130
(audience applauds)

00:01:58.130 --> 00:01:59.170
- So sweet.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.350
- You know, you throw a dog in anything

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.856
and people are gonna like it.

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:03.730
- Yeah.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:05.160
- I mean, I bark.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.767
I do, I full commit.

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:08.050
(Drew growls)
(audience laughs)

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:09.851
I get-
(Drew barks)

00:02:09.851 --> 00:02:11.310
(Drew pants)
(audience laughs)

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.607
I go all the way!

00:02:13.441 --> 00:02:15.281
And they didn't call
me back for the sequel!

00:02:15.281 --> 00:02:16.453
(audience applauds)

00:02:16.453 --> 00:02:18.671
- This is an injustice. Outrage.

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.337
- Whoever is at the
studio right now is like,

00:02:20.337 --> 00:02:21.937
"That little..."

00:02:21.937 --> 00:02:25.212
(audience laughs)

00:02:25.212 --> 00:02:28.270
Okay, in our last story, moving on.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.890
Apparently, I haven't moved on.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.600
- [Ross] No!
(audience laughs)

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.610
- There's a dilemma that recently came

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.960
in to the advice column at USA Today.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.880
Someone wrote in to say

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.650
three of their friends in their group

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:43.700
are notoriously tardy or late

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.540
for every hangout, party and occasion.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:48.110
So for a recent night out,

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.330
the punctual friends told the late friends

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:52.080
that the event started at 9PM,

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.380
where the real start time was 10.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:56.450
This time, the friends actually, weirdly,

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:59.260
made it a concerted
effort to show up early.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.120
They got there at 8:30,
waited an hour and a half,

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.840
and were cranky and furious about it

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:04.800
the rest of the night.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.222
And now these friends
are no longer talking.

00:03:07.222 --> 00:03:08.055
(Ross gasps)

00:03:08.055 --> 00:03:09.530
And the letter writer wants to know

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.660
who was in the wrong?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:15.110
Who here is notoriously late?

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.870
Raise your hands, do it.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.760
Recognize it in yourself.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.550
It's a flaw, and a selfish one.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.140
And horrible, I see you
leaning into your friend

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.400
and whispering in her-
(audience laughs)

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.570
Raise it!

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:30.550
Just admit it right now that
you're a bad, naughty person.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:31.610
(audience laughs)

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.780
We are in the wrong.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.210
The late people are in the wrong.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.200
That's all I have to say.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.551
- So you are one of those people, who-

00:03:37.551 --> 00:03:38.563
- Yes.

00:03:38.563 --> 00:03:40.330
I try not to be.
(audience laughs)

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.650
I try not to be.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.483
I...

00:03:44.196 --> 00:03:46.140
I am working on it.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.070
I'm getting better.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.913
I've improved immensely.

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.534
I really have, there is room for hope.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:54.670
(audience laughs)

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:58.020
And I can tell you that it
is terrible time management.

00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:00.030
I've put on an Instagram thing

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:01.320
that's like,

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.580
Michael from "The Office,"

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.577
and it says "I'm running at 9:10

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:07.920
"hoping to make it to the office by 9AM."

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.022
- [Ross] Uh-huh.
(audience laughs)

00:04:10.022 --> 00:04:11.430
- And so I'm working on it.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:13.770
And people who are late are in the wrong.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:14.820
But I am working on it.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.490
And I am sickened!
(audience applauds)

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:17.323
With myself.

00:04:19.052 --> 00:04:19.969
- You know,

00:04:21.917 --> 00:04:24.150
you know, there's...

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:25.460
There's a quote I like

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:28.030
from the famous poet, Kim Zolciak,

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.935
who said "Don't Be Tardy
for the Party," okay?

00:04:30.935 --> 00:04:32.550
(audience laughs)

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:36.120
Remind yourself of that next time.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.453
- I know, it's gotten better.

00:04:37.453 --> 00:04:41.090
I'm telling you, all of
us who raised our hands,

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:42.633
we can fix this.

00:04:43.778 --> 00:04:46.130
(audience laughs)

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.520
- I believe that you can.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:49.610
- [Drew] I have improved.

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:51.677
- No, that was my audition for the next...

00:04:51.677 --> 00:04:53.270
- "Beverly Hills Chihuahua!"
- "Beverly Hills Chiahuahua."

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.020
- How did I do? Was I believable?

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.280
- Put some panting and a ruff in there.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:59.436
Say we're going to break in a dog voice.

00:04:59.436 --> 00:05:01.279
- Rrr, we'll be right back. Rrr.

00:05:01.279 --> 00:05:02.716
(Drew laughs)
(audience applauds)

00:05:02.716 --> 00:05:05.299
(upbeat music)

